Package: simling
Title: Simulated Linguistic Data for Teaching Statistics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Massimiliano", "Canzi", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "massimiliano.canzi@uni-konstanz.de",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6124-0321"))
Description: Simulated data sets for teaching statistics to linguists, from
    phonetics, phonology, prosody, psycholinguistics, syntax, morphology,
    semantics and pragmatics, conversation analysis, corpus linguistics,
    sociolinguistics, dialectology, bilingualism, second language research,
    language acquisition, sign language, forensic speech science, historical
    linguistics and typology, and from languages including German, Italian,
    Portuguese, Hungarian, Mandarin, Cantonese, Korean and German Sign
    Language. Responses include continuous measures, reaction times, binary
    and multi-category outcomes, ratings, counts, censored ages, effect sizes,
    eye-tracking and EEG measures and time series, in data sets from 18 to
    over 20,000 rows, plus one messy export for data cleaning. Each data set
    comes with the code that generated it, so the true effects are known. A
    function lists the data sets by branch, language, size and response.
